  "remaining": [
    "Overall photographic fidelity remains unaccepted. The full tower still has overly regular storey/bracket/window rhythms and less specific historic carving than HD05.",
    "The actual four-piece cloud cassette is a declared different-source composition. Its outline, mirrored rhythm and gilt/wood finish are not the photographed original; only actual component geometry is recovered.",
    "Lower paired-curl end ornaments and thin header/post filigree are still schematic/repetitive. Main boot petals, carved cheek curves and copper edge work remain authored interpretations.",
    "Wood now has red/brown/gray-red roles, real gouged channels and end grain, but grain/age variation and shadow warmth remain unlike the reference in several regions.",
    "Kiln seam stagger and handworked rafters reduce coincident checker seams; ceramic flower-cap geometry and visible eave repetition are still too regular.",
    "The inherited onigawara r12c, sky/cloud placement and dense green canopy remain strongly different from the reference.",
    "A single actual local raster reflection probe is used for metals, with a finite sunlit court and the existing native bounce proxies. This is not traced GI or Cycles material equivalence. No new motion or Cycles frame was rendered."
  ]
